# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Smart Digital Queue Management System — Required Environment Variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This file is safe to commit to source control — it contains NO real secrets.
# It documents the variable names that must be present in .env.local
# (which is git-ignored and must NEVER be committed).
#
# ── HOW TO SET UP ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   1. Copy this file:  cp .env.example .env.local
#   2. Open .env.local and replace each placeholder with your real value.
#   3. Restart the Vite dev server so it picks up the new values:
#        npm run dev
#
# ── WHERE TO FIND THESE VALUES ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   • Log in to https://supabase.com
#   • Select your project
#   • Go to:  Settings (gear icon) → API
#
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#     Label on the page:  "Project URL"
#     Example format:     https://xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
#
#   VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
#     Label on the page:  "Project API keys" → "anon" / "public" key
#     Example format:     eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
#
# ── SECURITY RULES ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   ✅  Use ONLY the anon/publishable key in frontend code.
#   ❌  NEVER paste the "service_role" key here or anywhere in the frontend.
#       The service_role key bypasses Row Level Security and must only
#       be used in a secure backend environment (server, Edge Function, etc.).
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.your-anon-key-here
